PREAMBLE

Unlike the Lacspace Free Licence that covers Lacspace's software packages, this
package contains Lacspace's actual brand identity. Lacspace shares it openly so
that anyone can represent, reference and integrate with Lacspace correctly — but
the Brand Assets are not placed in the public domain and may not be altered or
used to imply a relationship that does not exist. The canonical, always-current
text of these brand guidelines is maintained at https://lacspace.com/brand

PERMITTED USE

You may, free of charge, worldwide and without needing to ask:

  1. Use the Brand Assets to link to, refer to, or identify Lacspace and its
     products and services.
  2. State truthfully that your product, content or project works with,
     integrates with, is built on, or is compatible with Lacspace, and use the
     mark to do so.
  3. Display the Brand Assets in articles, documentation, presentations,
     directories, "powered by" and "works with" notices, and similar editorial
     or informational contexts.
  4. Reproduce the Brand Assets unmodified at any size, in any of the colour
     variants provided, and use the marks generated by this package's code.

CONDITIONS

  a. Do not alter the marks. Do not recolour the gradient, redraw, distort,
     rotate, add effects, or combine the mark with other elements to form a new
     logo. Use the provided variants. (The generator functions in this package
     produce approved variants and are permitted output.)
  b. Do not imply endorsement, sponsorship, partnership or affiliation with
     Lacspace that has not been agreed in writing.
  c. Do not use the Brand Assets as, or as part of, your own product name,
     logo, trademark, domain name, or company identity.
  d. Do not use the Brand Assets in a false, misleading, disparaging, or
     unlawful manner, or in a way that could cause confusion about the source
     of a product or service.
  e. Respect the clear-space and minimum-size guidance included with this
     package and at https://lacspace.com/brand

